# Default: treat every file as text with LF line endings unless overridden
# below. A catch-all is required because per-extension enumeration silently
# missed *.go / *.rs / *.kt etc., letting Windows check them out as CRLF —
# which breaks gofmt and the byte-for-byte sync gates (QA finding F1).
* text=auto eol=lf

# Ensure shell scripts always use LF line endings (required for Docker/Linux)
*.sh text eol=lf

# Ensure Python scripts use LF
*.py text eol=lf

# C/C++ source files
*.c text eol=lf
*.cpp text eol=lf
*.h text eol=lf
*.hpp text eol=lf

# C# files
*.cs text eol=lf
*.csproj text eol=lf
*.sln text eol=lf
*.props text eol=lf
*.targets text eol=lf
*.runsettings text eol=lf

# CMake files
CMakeLists.txt text eol=lf
*.cmake text eol=lf

# JSON files (required for byte-for-byte sync across runtimes — Windows CRLF would break sha256 gate)
*.json text eol=lf

# Docker files
Dockerfile* text eol=lf
.dockerignore text eol=lf

# Windows scripts (keep CRLF)
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Gradle wrapper (must stay POSIX LF; otherwise `./gradlew` fails on Linux/macOS)
gradlew text eol=lf
*/gradlew text eol=lf
gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.properties text eol=lf

# Gradle wrapper jar is binary
*.jar binary

# CHANGELOG.md: keep BOTH sides of a conflicting hunk instead of failing.
#
# The file is append-only within `## [Unreleased]`, and every PR adds entries
# to the same few lines, so any two concurrent PRs conflict there and nothing
# else. Measured during the timing work: nine open PRs all touching
# CHANGELOG.md meant each merge put the other eight into CONFLICTING, and the
# resolution was mechanical every single time -- keep both sides, in order.
#
# `union` is git's built-in low-level driver for exactly this: on a hunk both
# sides changed, it concatenates their lines rather than writing conflict
# markers. Verified on a scratch repo: rebasing a branch that prepends one
# entry onto a branch that prepended another yields both, in order, with zero
# conflict markers.
#
# The trade-off is that a genuine CONTRADICTION -- two PRs editing the same
# existing sentence differently -- now merges silently to both versions
# instead of stopping. That is acceptable here and only here: entries are
# additive prose, the result is reviewed in the PR diff, and
# `scripts/check_changelog_format.py` / `check_changelog_unreleased.py` /
# `check_migration_changelog_parity.py` still run on the merged text. Do NOT
# extend `merge=union` to source files, where the same behaviour would
# silently produce code that compiles and is wrong.
#
# Scope: the pattern has no leading slash, so it matches CHANGELOG.md at ANY
# depth -- the root file plus the three package changelogs
# (src/python/g2p, src/wasm/g2p, src/wasm/openjtalk-web). That is intended:
# all four have the same append-only [Unreleased] shape. CHANGELOG-archive.md
# is deliberately NOT matched; it is historical and a conflict there means
# something is rewriting the past, which should stop and be looked at.
CHANGELOG.md merge=union
